// Disables Go's automatic vendor mode for this module.
//
// `company-os-starter/vendor/` is the *Python* PyYAML tree that `install.sh:91`
// ships and points PYTHONPATH at — it is not a Go vendor directory. Once
// `go.mod` acquired its first dependency, the Go toolchain saw `vendor/` at the
// module root, enabled `-mod=vendor`, and failed every build looking for a
// `vendor/modules.txt` that must never exist.
//
// Do NOT run `go mod vendor` here: it would rebuild `vendor/` from scratch and
// delete PyYAML, breaking `bin/company-os` and `install.sh`.
//
// This file retires itself. R-9.3 deletes `vendor/` at cutover, after which Go
// has nothing to misinterpret and `go.work` can be removed.
go 1.22

use .
